1
00:00:00,300 --> 00:00:02,830
一只老鼠，头顶戴着一台显微镜，
A mouse wears a microscope on its head

2
00:00:02,830 --> 00:00:03,960
只有1克重。
that weighs just 1 gram.

3
00:00:03,960 --> 00:00:04,820
它一边跑，
While it runs around,

4
00:00:04,820 --> 00:00:08,570
科学家一边同时看它8500多个神经元在闪。
scientists watch more than 8,500 of its neurons flash at once.

5
00:00:08,570 --> 00:00:10,780
今天的问题：看老鼠的大脑，
Today's question: to look inside a mouse's brain,

6
00:00:10,780 --> 00:00:13,630
为什么非得让它自己背着显微镜跑？
why make the mouse carry the microscope?

7
00:00:13,630 --> 00:00:14,880
认识一下米米。
Meet Mimi.

8
00:00:14,880 --> 00:00:17,670
米米是一只小鼠，今天它当主角。
Mimi is a mouse, and today Mimi is the star.

9
00:00:17,670 --> 00:00:20,000
这台显微镜叫 Airscope，
The microscope is called Airscope,

10
00:00:20,000 --> 00:00:22,740
是清华大学和解放军总医院的团队做的。
built by teams at Tsinghua University and the PLA General Hospital.

11
00:00:22,740 --> 00:00:23,770
10月19日，
On October 19,

12
00:00:23,770 --> 00:00:25,500
它登上了《自然》杂志。
it was published in Nature.

13
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:27,390
先说神经元怎么“看”：
First, how do you even see neurons?

14
00:00:27,390 --> 00:00:29,220
它们平时根本看不见。
Normally you can't.

15
00:00:29,220 --> 00:00:30,930
科学家常用的办法是，
A common trick is to give neurons

16
00:00:30,930 --> 00:00:33,600
让神经元带上一种会发光的蛋白。
a protein that glows.

17
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:35,780
神经元一放电，就亮一下，
When a neuron fires, it lights up,

18
00:00:35,780 --> 00:00:38,080
像一栋楼的灯一盏盏开关。
like windows in a building switching on and off.

19
00:00:38,080 --> 00:00:39,360
拍下这些闪光，
Film those flashes,

20
00:00:39,360 --> 00:00:41,690
就等于偷看大脑在说什么。
and you're eavesdropping on the brain.

21
00:00:41,690 --> 00:00:44,750
可老办法常常是：把老鼠的头固定住，
But the old way often means holding the mouse's head still

22
00:00:44,750 --> 00:00:46,480
放在大显微镜底下。
under a big microscope.

23
00:00:46,480 --> 00:00:48,240
就像让你一动不动躺着，
It's like lying perfectly still

24
00:00:48,240 --> 00:00:50,290
还要求你“自然地”逛街。
and being told to go shopping naturally.

25
00:00:50,290 --> 00:00:51,500
反转一：重量。
Twist one: weight.

26
00:00:51,500 --> 00:00:54,030
一只小鼠，大约只有二三十克。
A mouse weighs only about 20 to 30 grams.

27
00:00:54,030 --> 00:00:56,310
常见的头戴显微镜超过3克，
Typical head-mounted microscopes weigh over 3 grams,

28
00:00:56,310 --> 00:00:58,540
差不多是体重的十分之一。
about a tenth of its body weight.

29
00:00:58,540 --> 00:01:01,360
我们估算一下：换成60公斤的人，
Our rough estimate: for a 60-kilogram person,

30
00:01:01,360 --> 00:01:03,770
等于头顶扛着6公斤的西瓜。
that's a 6-kilogram watermelon on your head.

31
00:01:03,770 --> 00:01:04,960
现在只有1克，
Now it's 1 gram,

32
00:01:04,960 --> 00:01:07,130
大约相当于人顶一大瓶水。
more like balancing a big bottle of water.

33
00:01:07,130 --> 00:01:08,160
反转二：线。
Twist two: wires.

34
00:01:08,160 --> 00:01:10,330
很多老设备要拖着一根线。
Many older devices trail a cable.

35
00:01:10,330 --> 00:01:11,560
线会缠，会绊，
Cables tangle and trip.

36
00:01:11,560 --> 00:01:14,500
几只老鼠一起玩，就打成一团毛线。
Put a few mice together and you get a ball of yarn.

37
00:01:14,500 --> 00:01:16,610
Airscope 是无线的，
Airscope is wireless.

38
00:01:16,610 --> 00:01:18,850
在头上先把图压缩，再发出去。
It compresses images on its head, then sends them out.

39
00:01:18,850 --> 00:01:20,680
200万像素的传感器，
A 2-megapixel sensor,

40
00:01:20,680 --> 00:01:22,120
只用了4片镜片。
with just 4 lenses.

41
00:01:22,120 --> 00:01:23,170
视野6毫米，
A 6-millimeter field of view,

42
00:01:23,170 --> 00:01:25,030
能看清一个一个细胞。
sharp enough to see single cells.

43
00:01:25,030 --> 00:01:28,070
一只老鼠同时记下8500多个神经元，
Over 8,500 neurons recorded in one mouse at once,

44
00:01:28,070 --> 00:01:29,880
是同类设备的25倍。
25 times more than similar devices.

45
00:01:29,880 --> 00:01:31,380
反转三，最烧脑：
Twist three, the brain-bender:

46
00:01:31,380 --> 00:01:33,940
看到更多，为什么这么重要？
why does seeing more matter so much?

47
00:01:33,940 --> 00:01:36,310
因为行为不是一个神经元干的，
Because behavior isn't done by one neuron.

48
00:01:36,310 --> 00:01:38,290
是成千上万个一起合唱。
It's thousands singing together.

49
00:01:38,290 --> 00:01:39,520
只听一个人唱，
Listen to just one singer,

50
00:01:39,520 --> 00:01:41,210
你听不出是哪首歌。
and you can't tell the song.

51
00:01:41,210 --> 00:01:43,420
团队在5平方米的“小区”里，
In a 5-square-meter habitat,

52
00:01:43,420 --> 00:01:45,600
同时记录好几只老鼠的大脑。
the team recorded several mice at the same time.

53
00:01:45,600 --> 00:01:48,460
还让它们在有32个出口的大迷宫里，
They also let mice roam freely

54
00:01:48,460 --> 00:01:49,590
自己随便逛。
in a big maze with 32 dead ends.

55
00:01:49,590 --> 00:01:51,860
老鼠自由社交、自由探索，
When mice can socialize and explore freely,

56
00:01:51,860 --> 00:01:53,310
大脑才说真话。
their brains tell the truth.

57
00:01:53,310 --> 00:01:55,570
我们猜：看懂动物怎么找路，
Our guess: understanding how animals find their way

58
00:01:55,570 --> 00:01:57,770
也许能帮机器人学会探索。
might help robots learn to explore.

59
00:01:57,770 --> 00:01:59,960
友情提示：这是动物实验，
Friendly fine print: this is animal research.

60
00:01:59,960 --> 00:02:02,640
看的是大脑表层，不是读心术。
It sees the brain's surface layer, not your thoughts.

61
00:02:02,640 --> 00:02:03,950
离用在人身上，
Using it on people

62
00:02:03,950 --> 00:02:04,820
还很远。
is still a long way off.

63
00:02:04,820 --> 00:02:06,580
团队说，以后还想用它
The team says they hope to use it

64
00:02:06,580 --> 00:02:08,100
研究免疫和肿瘤。
for immunity and cancer research, too.

65
00:02:08,100 --> 00:02:09,860
米米表示：帽子很轻，
Mimi says: the hat is light.

66
00:02:09,860 --> 00:02:11,790
就是脑子一直在闪。
It's just that the brain keeps flashing.

